# Format:
# METHOD  TYPE  CODE  VALUE  [MODIFIER]
#
# COLUMN DEFINITIONS:
# 1. METHOD:    The internal Kobo function to call.
# 2. TYPE:      The Linux Input Event Type. Usually 'EV_KEY' for buttons or 'EV_ABS' for joysticks.
# 3. CODE:      The specific button code. Examples: KEY_VOLUMEUP, KEY_VOLUMEDOWN, BTN_A, BTN_B
# 4. VALUE:     The state of the button.
#               1 = Press (Trigger immediately when button goes down)
#               0 = Release (Trigger when button is let go)
# 5. MODIFIER:  (Optional) Time-based filtering.
#               SHORT = Only trigger if held for less than 500ms.
#               LONG  = Only trigger if held for more than 500ms.
#               (If omitted, action triggers on any duration).
#
# ! IMPORTANT RULE FOR LONG/SHORT PRESS !
# If you use the MODIFIER column (SHORT or LONG), the VALUE column MUST be 0.
# Why? To measure how long you held a button, the system must wait until you
# release it. If you use '1' (Press), the action will fire immediately.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Short press turns the page forward
nextPage EV_KEY KEY_VOLUMEUP 0 SHORT

# Long press (held >500ms) goes back
prevPage EV_KEY KEY_VOLUMEUP 0 LONG
